From: Michael Daniels <mdaniels5757@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: refresh snapshots for Pygments 2.21

Compact test-only equivalent of the snapshot changes in upstream issue 4209:
https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues/4209
https://gist.github.com/mdaniels5757/d2d48e8a5478b7b875b454b1237d3874/069a45fdaffba77b377b59e8c540a035b71ee82c

Pygments now recognizes Python builtins such as iter and next.
Visible text is unchanged; change only the four builtin token colors.
Each of the seven resulting fixtures was checked against the upstream patch.
Runtime dependency constraints and runtime code are unchanged.

